[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: ngspice Corpus Compatibility Track

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-001
TITLE: Full corpus inventory
STATEMENT: >>>
The project shall inventory every recognized circuit fixture in a user-provided ngspice checkout without modifying that checkout, recording path, content hash, lexical feature markers and an explicit compatibility status.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: scripts/Inventory-Ngspice.cs. Initial observed baseline: 118 test circuit files at local revision e8285746c.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-002
TITLE: No implied full compatibility
STATEMENT: >>>
Each ngspice corpus fixture shall be classified as candidate_basic, supported, unsupported or future_feature. A fixture may be marked supported only after it executes against a documented result oracle.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The corpus is a roadmap and regression source, not a blanket behavioral compatibility claim.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-003
TITLE: External corpus integrity
STATEMENT: >>>
Compatibility tooling shall treat the ngspice checkout as read-only and shall retain source attribution and license context for copied fixtures or result oracles.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
The current checkout reports a mixed license context with Modified BSD as the general test/example baseline; inspect upstream COPYING before copying any additional material.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-004
TITLE: One hundred-family compatibility campaign
STATEMENT: >>>
The project shall maintain a stable, machine-readable campaign of exactly one hundred named ngspice compatibility feature families. Each family shall have an explicit status selected from supported, import_only, supported_api_only, planned, future or unsupported. A status shall not imply compatibility beyond its stated scope.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: scripts/Plan-NgspiceFeatureFamilies.cs. The list deliberately separates deck import, public typed API capability, planned work and permanently unsupported interactive/plugin mechanisms.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-005
TITLE: Independent executable oracle
STATEMENT: >>>
When a curated fixture is promoted to supported, verification shall compare a documented observable against an independently executed ngspice batch result or another documented analytic oracle. The verifier shall preserve the command, executable identity, fixture hash and tolerance as evidence.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: scripts/Run-NgspiceOracle.cs creates a fixture-hash-named build directory and emits executable path, fixture hash, exit code and complete batch log. scripts/Compare-NgspiceOracle.cs compares the named i(V1) observable for the curated res_simple fixture at a 1e-12 tolerance. This prevents importer acceptance from being mistaken for numerical compatibility.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-006
TITLE: Safe compact DC-source import
STATEMENT: >>>
The bounded ngspice importer shall normalize DC <value> and DC=<value> source forms and inline semicolon comments. It shall reject source waveform or AC tails that it cannot represent, rather than silently reducing them to DC values.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/netlist.rs parse_ngspice_basic. Verification: tests/ngspice_compat.rs compact form and waveform rejection tests.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-007
TITLE: Pulse waveform semantics
STATEMENT: >>>
The typed transient API shall represent a bounded periodic pulse waveform with finite levels, nonnegative delay/rise/fall/width, a positive period and no pulse phase duration exceeding that period.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/waveform.rs Waveform::Pulse. Verification: tests/ngspice_compat.rs exact plateau/edge and invalid-period tests.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: NGC-008
TITLE: Bounded transient-deck lowering
STATEMENT: >>>
The ngspice importer shall lower exactly one two-value .tran directive into a typed configured transient request. Optional transient fields outside that profile shall fail explicitly rather than being discarded.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: src/netlist.rs import_ngspice_request. Verification: tests/ngspice_compat.rs transient lowering test.
<<<
